Let $f(x)=- 2 x^{2} - x - 1$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=- 4 x - 1\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(1\\right)=- 4 \\left(1\\right) - 1=-5\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-5\\right)}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-4\\right)&=\\frac{1}{5}\\left(x-\\left(1\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{x}{5}+\\left(- \\frac{1}{5}\\right)+\\left(-4\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{x}{5} - \\frac{21}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $a=\\frac{1}{5}$ and $b=- \\frac{21}{5}$." 13194139547568 17592186576411 true] [17592186760922 1068 #edb/ref 17592186760912 13194139547568 17592186576411 true] [17592186760922 1068 #edb/ref 17592186760917 13194139547568 17592186576411 true] [17592186760922 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139547568 17592186576411 true] [17592186760922 1071 "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=2 x^{2} - 2 x + 2$ at $\\left(2,6\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $y=ax+b$.\n\n$a=$ {{slope}}\n\n$b=$ {{intercept}}" 13194139547568 17592186576411 true] [17592186760922 1072 #uuid "c80c6849-c2ca-5979-b8db-38c19e3845b0" 13194139547568 17592186576411 true] [17592186760922 1074 "Let $f(x)=2 x^{2} - 2 x + 2$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=4 x - 2\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(2\\right)=4 \\left(2\\right) - 2=6\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(6\\right)}=- \\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(6\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{6}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{6}+\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)+\\left(6\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{19}{3} - \\frac{x}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $a=- \\frac{1}{6}$ and $b=\\frac{19}{3}$." 13194139547568 17592186576411 true] [17592186760923 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" 131941395475